==English==

===Etymology===
{{etydate|1559}}; {{bor+|en|la|dēlīneātus|nocap=1}}, {{glossary|perfect}} {{glossary|passive}} {{glossary|participle}} of {{m|la|dēlīneo||to sketch out, to delineate}} (see {{af|en|-ate|id1=verb|pos1=verb-forming suffix}} and {{af|en|-ate|id1=adjective|pos1=adjective-forming suffix}}), from {{m|la|dē-}} + {{m|la|līnea||line}} + {{m|la|-ō|id=denominative|pos=verb-forming suffix}}. Regular participial usage of the [[#Adjective|adjective]] up until {{w|Early Modern English}}. 

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|en|/dɪˈlɪniːeɪt/|a=UK}}
* {{audio|en|LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-delineate.wav|a=Southern England}}

===Verb===
{{en-verb}}

# To [[sketch out]], [[draw]] or [[trace]] an [[outline]].
# To [[depict]], [[represent]] with pictures.
# To [[describe]] or depict with words or gestures.
# To [[outline#English: summarize|outline]] or [[mark out]].

====Synonyms====
* {{sense|to mark the limits or boundaries}} {{l|en|demark}}, {{l|en|demarcate}}, {{l|en|delimit}}

